# Skill: claude-md-audit

Cursor adapter for the `claude-md-audit` skill. Full procedure (single source of truth):
`.claude/skills/claude-md-audit/SKILL.md` in this repo.

## When To Use

The user names `claude-md-audit`, asks to audit instruction files, or session quality has drifted.
In camels_ru, `AGENTS.md` is the cross-agent source of truth and `CLAUDE.md` is a thin `@AGENTS.md`
importer; lookup tables live in `AGENTS_REFERENCE.md`/`CLAUDE_REFERENCE.md`.

## When Not To Use

Routine doc edits, scientific manuscript review, or generic "improve the docs" requests.

## Workflow

Read both `AGENTS.md` (SoT) and the `CLAUDE.md` layer plus their reference files. Flag stale facts,
verbosity, drift-encouraging rules, and **layering violations** (shared rule in `CLAUDE.md` instead
of `AGENTS.md`; `CLAUDE.md` bloat). Findings first.

## Output Handling

Edit the source layer: shared rules → `AGENTS.md`; Claude-only runtime → `CLAUDE.md` (keep it thin);
lookup material → the `*_REFERENCE.md` files. Prefer fewer high-value edits over many cosmetic ones.

## Safety Constraints

No scoring systems or personality text unless asked. Verify facts against the repo before editing.
Do not expose secrets. Do not apply child-agent changes automatically.
